# Line endings are LF in the repository, and LF in every working tree.
#
# skills/visualkan-wizard/references/controls.md is generated by
# `visualkan sync-version` and is also committed. A test compares it against
# what controlsReport() produces, and that output uses \n. Git's Windows
# default, core.autocrlf=true, rewrote the file to CRLF on checkout, so the
# suite failed on a fresh clone while passing on any machine where the file
# had been regenerated locally. Found by running the tests in a clean worktree,
# not by reading them.
* text=auto eol=lf
